From 36b2a17110b5eb008c8fafff8a7d0ff8ce5892b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 01:20:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Open prepared handoffs where the atomic no-follow store
 exists

The gate's original reason was missing atomic no-follow snapshot-index
publication. The V2 delta implements it on Unix, so the gate now opens on
Unix and stays closed elsewhere, still without any configuration or
environment-variable bypass. The ten prepare-dependent tests run on Unix;
fail-closed assertions remain for platforms without the store. Tool and
reminder text now explain prepare instead of forbidding it.
---
